# What omni_virus issues, and where its 12% cross-check gap comes from.
# trn1.2xlarge, 2026-09-22 16:05-16:14 UTC, tools/omni_flops.py at c9538b1 (hash-checked
# on the host). Captures the chain at tile 2048 and the pinned 8192 with neuron-profile and
# prints the hardware model_flops against each candidate analytic formula.
#
# ANSWER: the compiler lowers the chain cumsum onto the Tensor Engine and the monitor counts
# it. The extra is exactly tile^3/2 at 8192 (ratio 1.125) and exactly 2*tile^3 at 2048
# (ratio 1.500) -- shape-dependent, so one formula cannot absorb it, which is why the
# expected ratio is declared per workload instead (registry.MONITOR_OVER_KERNEL_EXPECTED).


